commit f725d7dcb	a few blocks on a point read (9 / 13 / 17 to 9 / 11 / 15 for an equality, a short range and an IN list of 16 keys); no statement of the registry isolates the read of the directory header, and the time of no statement moves; test/sql/col_gorder_point.sql counts the blocks
commit 95bf906bf	the planner price of the keys of an IN list on an order array; the point_scattered_N cases plan the point directory in the builds before and after (60 keys: 2.7 million instructions and 561 against 563 blocks in both), so they do not show it; test/sql/col_gorder_point.sql covers the lists
commit cf7a0678d	a plan choice between the scan and the b-tree plan of one table; the b-tree variants of the registry are tables of their own, so no case shows it; test/sql/agg_unique_key_in_list.sql covers it
commit 672d457c2	the decode of a compact chunk costs 5.5 instructions an entry with AVX2 against 45 (a unit test and the tools/gquant microbenchmark); the statements that read compact chunks are order_layout_range and order_layout_offset_deep, whose time is not decode-bound
commit 570bd2526	the case wbuf_narrowest_condition_first shows no difference from PostgreSQL's plan at 300,000 rows (0.58 ms against 0.63 ms, 41 blocks each): the 1,203-block shape of the commit is not reproduced at this size; test/sql covers the rows
commit a3f3dfef0	a plan price (514 against 82 for k = ANY(300 keys) AND k = 7) held by test/sql; keys_in_few_256 runs the same plan as PostgreSQL at 300,000 rows (0.65 ms against 0.64 ms), so no case shows a gain
commit 466aa2f9f	a lateral top-1 over a key-cut grouped order array of 1,000,000 rows (24.2 to 17.8 million instructions, 2.6 to 2.0 ms) is a size no registry case runs at 300,000 rows; test/sql/col_gorder_group.sql checks the rows
commit 1148c0f74	2,000 hash partitions planned from a new connection, a statistics-sharing test; test/t/leaf_stats_shared.sh checks that every connection finds the records shared
commit 170199310	a planner price of the rows a lookup gets through a b-tree index; test/plan/bands.tsv, calibrate.tsv, planning.tsv and test/expected/agg_lookup_rows_read.out hold the plan choice of 140 entities of mid rank
commit f786fbc57	repairs the cost that 5ce93b74c added on every read of a kept batch set (116 to 43 blocks, 5,287,447 to 5,228,487 instructions on the narrow statement of a 15-page buffer); not a gain over a released version
commit c7468b07c	comment and option text only; no code path changes
commit ca46315a9	comment and option text only; the choice of the layout is not changed
commit 5ce93b74c	a repair of wrong rows after VACUUM in a development version that never shipped; its cost is measured: 69,711 instructions to stamp a buffer of 15 pages and 20,151 for each read that finds the set (0.5% of the page statement)
commit 9e574ccc6	CHANGELOG line written after the commit; case topn_offset_after_vacuum
commit 68f4de4d2	CHANGELOG line written after the commit; case distinct_on_latest_per_entity
commit f2178aebd	the cost of a probe that started over at each LATERAL row (80.8 to 55.9 thousand instructions by callgrind) is part of what lateral_top1_kept_source measures: 200 probes over 300,000 rows take 8.3 million instructions and 1.01 ms (a b-tree 6.8 million, 0.79 ms). The commit alone, built with and without it on the same data (200 probes, key_cut grouped order array, 300,000 rows): 21.1 to 17.8 million instructions, 2.4 to 2.1 ms in the same 3,214 blocks (a b-tree 5.5 million, 0.6 ms)
commit 96387b908	a test commit: a counter (sift._test_col_gdead_stats, third column) that pins that the cut of an OFFSET is taken, asserted by test/sql/agg_topn_offset_bulk.sql (30,000 to 40,000 entries cut for OFFSET 40,000, none with the cut off); it gives no speed of its own, and the OFFSET cases measure the statement
commit d446b8f67	a planner price held by test/sql/agg_join_filter_price.sql (failing first: the filtered join of 20 of 40,000 rows was the hash join, it stays the scan) and the plan matrix shape semi_expr_key; the commit's figures are costs and the time of the plan chosen, not a speed of a case
commit f23436160	held by test/sql/agg_topn_walk_refused.sql (failing first: 303 heap fetches for the latest row of an entity alone and per entity, 0 and 0 now, the rows equal the normal plan's); the LATERAL cases lateral_top1_text_filter and lateral_top1_kept_source run the statements
commit 6ff768eeb	a planner price held by test/sql/agg_par_cost.sql (the lookup, category and bucket classes, failing first: workers on the previous price) and agg_workers_guessed_keys.sql; the commit's times are the plan matrix's best of 25 runs
commit 079bb110e	held by test/sql/agg_exact_units_dirty.sql (failing first: the cost of a month's count with 5% of the pages dirty at the end is under twice the clean one, with 1 page in 20 dirty anywhere it is over twice); the plan matrix with the dirty dimension is the time proof
commit 478e9cb3b	a planner price held by test/sql/agg_topn_runs_filter.sql (failing first: the page of 5,000 of 300,000 rows with 10% passing is the scan and cheaper than the normal plan, and its price grows with the page); the commit's table is the cost against the time of the plan matrix
commit e7265c883	a planner price held by test/sql/agg_topn_walk_cost.sql (failing first, four booleans: the price of the walk follows the pass rate, 394 to 139 at 50%, 434 to 114 at 98%, the give-up boundary at 1%); col_topn_gorder now expects the array
commit eda053aae	CHANGELOG line written after the commit; case topn_offset_churn_text
commit 3d11cb1fb	a planner price of the probes of a repeated index scan held by test/sql/col_join_probe_price.sql (failing first: the arrival-order heap took the hash join, the same rows either way) and the plan matrix shape added with it
commit 74ccf0039	a planner price of the keys an index looks up in its order array held by test/sql/col_point_btree_price.sql (failing first: 500 keys took the sift_col index, the b-tree now, the same rows)
commit a33bd8e5f	a planner price of when the index paths of an aggregate over a few keys stay, held by test/sql/col_point_lookup_plan.sql (failing first: a column of 667 rows a key kept the index scan; 250,000 rows, the 216 rows of one day priced 76 against 187 for the aggregate scan and taking 1.4 ms against 0.55)
commit 1b3b58e06	repair of the baseline-ISA check (scripts/isa_check.sh): best level 30% fewer instructions per rank (116/356/676 to 83/251/475 at 4/16/32 words), the whole query under 0.2% (428.3 M to 427.6 M for 80 conjunctions); the scalar level counts by arithmetic, 151/487/935, more than the libgcc helper it replaces
commit 2d4d217b5	a planner price of the probes of a repeated index scan (the first unit looked up, the others walked, each heap row paid) held by test/sql/agg_topn_plan_keys.sql and col_list_equality.sql (failing first: both red on the tip; the nested loop of 124 rows a probe took 4 to 5 ms and 3,127 buffer hits where the top-N scan takes 1.4 ms and 50)
commit ab98e13a3	a planner price of the rows an index-only scan hands over (0.07 us plus 0.005 for each column of the index, measured 0.1 us for 3 columns, 0.22 for 28) held by test/sql/col_ios_full_price.sql (failing first: the hash join over a full index-only scan of 20,000 rows, 8 ms where the heap takes 0.8) and the join of 1,000 keys: 41 ms before, 7.8 ms after, 100,000 rows
commit 390c12b8b	CHANGELOG line written after the commit (the Added line of key_order); cases key_order_latest and key_order_offset
commit 43f9c7f63	a test-only floor (sift.table_max_segments 16 to 8, a setting that exists only in the testing build) so that tbl_writepath and tbl_bigtx reach the directory pressure with a quarter of the rows (71 s to 15 s and 11 s to 2 s of test time); the library a release ships is unchanged, held by test/sql/tbl_writepath.sql and tbl_bigtx.sql (failing with dir_pressure() always false)
commit 37eaaf50c	a test gate (sift.test_merge_gate) that holds a merge of the maintenance worker, replacing a sleep setting in the testing build; no statement gets faster, held by test/t/maint_lock.sh
commit 6f3edd674	which keys get the grouped order array by default is held by test/sql/col_gorder_autogroup_kinds.sql (a date of 365 values, a timestamp in heap order, an integer and a decimal, an entity of 20 rows and one of 2, a timestamp cut by key_cut, a table with nothing to group, a two-column index); the case lateral_latest_row_default runs the shape of the latest row of each entity
commit 11e5e77b6	a planner price that repairs two regression tests after the point directory became the default of an integer key: test/sql/col_point_dir.sql holds the plan of an equality on a boolean (the index scan priced by the row against the index-only scan) and test/sql/col_index_return_str.sql the plain index scan of the one-row lookups; the plan matrix has no flipped cell
